{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q411885","formula":"Cl₃Cr","hill":"Cl3Cr","elements":["Cl","Cr"],"composition":{"Cl":3.0,"Cr":1.0},"names":{"en":"Chromic chloride","ru":"Хлорид хрома(III)"},"descriptions":{"en":"Chromium(III) chloride (also called chromic chloride, or chromium trichloride) is an inorganic chemical compound with the chemical formula CrCl3. This crystalline salt forms several hydrates with the formula CrCl3·nH2O, among which are hydrates where n can be 5 (chromium(III) chloride pentahydrate CrCl3·5H2O) or 6 (chromium(III) chloride hexahydrate CrCl3·6H2O). The anhydrous compound with the formula CrCl3 are violet crystals, while the most common form of the chromium(III) chloride are the dark green crystals of hexahydrate, CrCl3·6H2O. Chromium chlorides find use as catalysts and as precursors to dyes for wool.","ru":"Хлори́д хро́ма(III) — неорганическое бинарное соединение хрома и хлора с формулой CrCl3, хромовая соль соляной кислоты."},"fame":34,"pubchemCid":24808,"mass":158.35,"charge":0,"smiles":"Cl[Cr](Cl)Cl","inchikey":"QSWDMMVNRMROPK-UHFFFAOYSA-K","iupac":"trichlorochromium","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-27630","atoms":20,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[6.0,0.0,0.0],[0.0,10.383,0.0],[-1.891,0.0,5.999]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":2.055,"y":3.46,"z":3.0,"el":"Cr"},{"x":2.055,"y":6.923,"z":3.0,"el":"Cr"},{"x":0.987,"y":1.848,"z":1.665,"el":"Cl"},{"x":3.123,"y":1.848,"z":4.334,"el":"Cl"},{"x":4.196,"y":0.0,"z":1.659,"el":"Cl"},{"x":4.196,"y":10.383,"z":1.659,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-0.087,"y":0.0,"z":4.34,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-0.087,"y":10.383,"z":4.34,"el":"Cl"},{"x":0.987,"y":8.535,"z":1.665,"el":"Cl"},{"x":3.123,"y":8.535,"z":4.334,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-0.945,"y":8.652,"z":3.0,"el":"Cr"},{"x":5.055,"y":8.652,"z":3.0,"el":"Cr"},{"x":-0.945,"y":1.731,"z":3.0,